      "aiValidity": null,
      "body": "## Vulnerability details\n\n`previewMint` computes the cost of minting shares using ceiling (round-up) arithmetic at two steps:\n\n```solidity\n// ProgressiveCurve.sol L131-132\nUD60x18 area     = sub(PCMath.squareUp(sNext), PCMath.square(s)); // squareUp = ceiling\nUD60x18 assetsUD = PCMath.mulUp(area, HALF_SLOPE);                // mulUp    = ceiling\n```\n\nThe curve invariant requires `totalAssets == HALF_SLOPE * square(totalShares)`. Ceiling rounding breaks this invariant on every mint: after any `previewMint`-routed deposit, `totalAssets` is strictly greater than `HALF_SLOPE * square(totalShares)`.\n\n`previewWithdraw` then attempts:\n\n```solidity\n// ProgressiveCurve.sol L153-155\nUD60x18 deduct = PCMath.divUp(wrap(assets), HALF_SLOPE);\nUD60x18 inner  = sub(PCMath.square(s), deduct);  // <-- PANIC here\n```\n\nPRB-Math's `sub` performs an unchecked subtraction on unsigned fixed-point numbers. When the invariant is broken, `divUp(totalAssets, HALF_SLOPE) > square(totalShares)`, so `deduct > square(s)`. The subtraction underflows and the transaction reverts with `ARITHMETIC_OVERFLOW (0x11)`.\n\nThe identical structure is present in `OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol` at L160:\n\n```solidity\n// OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol L136-137 (previewMint)\nUD60x18 area     = sub(PCMath.squareUp(sNext), PCMath.square(s));\nUD60x18 assetsUD = PCMath.mulUp(area, HALF_SLOPE);\n\n// OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol L158-160 (previewWithdraw)\nUD60x18 deduct = PCMath.divUp(wrap(assets), HALF_SLOPE);\nUD60x18 inner  = sub(PCMath.square(s), deduct);  // <-- identical PANIC\n```\n\n### Concrete state walk (SLOPE=2e18, HALF_SLOPE=1e18)\n\n```\nInitial state: totalShares = 1e18, totalAssets = 1e18\n\npreviewMint(1 share, totalShares=1e18, totalAssets=1e18):\n  s    = 1e18\n  sNext = 1e18 + 1\n  squareUp(1e18+1) = ceil((1e18+1)^2 / 1e18) = 1e18 + 3\n  square(1e18)     = 1e18\n  area      = 3\n  assetsUD  = mulUp(3, 1e18) = 3\n  cost      = 3\n\nNew vault state: totalShares = 1e18+1, totalAssets = 1e18+3\nInvariant check: square(1e18+1) = 1e18+2\n                 HALF_SLOPE * square(totalShares) = 1e18+2\n                 totalAssets = 1e18+3  >  1e18+2  -- INVARIANT BROKEN\n\npreviewWithdraw(1e18+3 assets, totalAssets=1e18+3, totalShares=1e18+1):\n  deduct = divUp(1e18+3, 1e18) = 1e18+3\n  inner  = sub(square(1e18+1)=1e18+2, 1e18+3)  --> PANIC(0x11)\n```\n\nEach sequential 1-share mint accumulates exactly 1 asset of irrecoverable excess. After N such mints, exactly N assets are permanently unwithdrawable via the asset-based path. The excess compounds for every subsequent small-share mint from a large `totalShares` base.\n\n### Regression note\n\nThe prior Diligence audit (Oct 2025, Finding 5.5) identified a rounding asymmetry in these curves and marked it Fixed in PR 111. The differential changes at `ProgressiveCurve.sol:L240` and `OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol:L247` subsequently re-introduced the invariant violation. This is a regression in the primary differential area.\n\n## Impact\n\nAny vault that processes a deposit through the `previewMint` path is permanently DoSed for all asset-based (`previewWithdraw`) exits:\n\n- Protocols and UIs implementing ERC4626-style `previewWithdraw` to compute share amounts before withdrawal will revert on every call.\n- Users cannot exit via the asset-denominated path. They must compute share amounts manually and use `previewRedeem` (shares-based), which remains functional.\n- The locked excess accumulates: N sequential 1-share mints lock N assets. For high-activity vaults with many small mints, the locked amount grows proportionally.\n- The DoS is irreversible without an upgrade: once `totalAssets > HALF_SLOPE * square(totalShares)`, every call to `previewWithdraw(totalAssets, ...)` panics until the invariant is externally restored.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nOption A (fix at the withdrawal side) — guard against invariant drift:\n\n```diff\n// ProgressiveCurve.sol ~L155 (identical change at OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol ~L160)\n-    UD60x18 inner = sub(PCMath.square(s), deduct);\n+    UD60x18 sq    = PCMath.square(s);\n+    UD60x18 inner = unwrap(deduct) <= unwrap(sq) ? sub(sq, deduct) : wrap(0);\n     UD60x18 sharesUD = sub(s, sqrt(inner));\n```\n\nWhen `deduct > square(s)`, `inner` clamps to `wrap(0)`. Because `sqrt(0) = 0`, the next line computes `sharesUD = sub(s, 0) = s`, so the function returns `totalShares` — effectively saying \"burn all shares to cover this amount.\" Callers receiving `totalShares` in response to a partial-withdrawal query should recognize the invariant is violated and fall back to `previewRedeem`.\n\nOption B (fix at the mint side) — maintain the invariant at source:\n\n```diff\n// ProgressiveCurve.sol L131-132 (identical change at OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol L136-137)\n-    UD60x18 area     = sub(PCMath.squareUp(sNext), PCMath.square(s));\n-    UD60x18 assetsUD = PCMath.mulUp(area, HALF_SLOPE);\n+    UD60x18 area     = sub(PCMath.square(sNext), PCMath.square(s));\n+    UD60x18 assetsUD = mul(area, HALF_SLOPE);\n```\n\nThis aligns `previewMint` with `previewDeposit`'s floor arithmetic, preserving `totalAssets == HALF_SLOPE * square(totalShares)` after every operation and eliminating the root cause. Note that switching from ceiling to floor means the contract collects slightly fewer assets per mint, which marginally favors depositors over the vault.\n\nOption B is preferred as it eliminates the invariant violation entirely rather than masking its effects.",
      "proofOfConcept": "## Proof of Concept\n\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\nimport { TransparentUpgradeableProxy } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol\";\nimport { OffsetProgressiveCurve } from \"src/protocol/curves/OffsetProgressiveCurve.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        _poc_ProgressiveCurve_previewWithdrawPanicAfterMint();\n        _poc_OffsetProgressiveCurve_previewWithdrawPanicAfterMint();\n    }\n\n    // HIGH-1: ProgressiveCurve.previewWithdraw panics after previewMint\n    //\n    // Root cause: previewMint computes cost via mulUp(squareUp(sNext) - square(s), HALF_SLOPE),\n    // where squareUp rounds the end-point UP. This makes totalAssets exceed HALF_SLOPE *\n    // square(totalShares) by 1 ULP per mint. previewWithdraw then computes\n    //     inner = sub(square(s), divUp(assets, HALF_SLOPE))\n    // where divUp(totalAssets, HALF_SLOPE) > square(totalShares) whenever the\n    // invariant is broken, causing PRB-Math sub() to panic (ARITHMETIC_OVERFLOW 0x11).\n    //\n    // State walk for SLOPE=2e18, HALF_SLOPE=1e18:\n    //   previewMint(1e18, 0, 0)        -> 1e18 assets   (exact, no rounding)\n    //   previewMint(1, 1e18, 1e18)     -> 3 assets\n    //     squareUp(1e18+1) = ceil((1e18+1)^2/1e18) = 1e18+3\n    //     square(1e18)     = 1e18\n    //     area = 3; mulUp(3, 1e18) = 3\n    //   vault: totalShares=1e18+1, totalAssets=1e18+3\n    //   INVARIANT BROKEN: 1e18+3 > square(1e18+1)=1e18+2\n    //\n    //   previewWithdraw(1e18+3, 1e18+3, 1e18+1):\n    //     s        = wrap(1e18+1)\n    //     deduct   = divUp(1e18+3, 1e18) = 1e18+3\n    //     square(s)= floor((1e18+1)^2/1e18) = 1e18+2\n    //     sub(1e18+2, 1e18+3) -> PANIC(0x11)\n    //\n    // Impact: every vault that settles a deposit through previewMint permanently loses\n    // the ability to execute a full asset-based withdrawal. Across N sequential 1-share\n    // mints the excess accumulates to N locked assets. The redeem (shares-based) path\n    // is unaffected, forcing users to compute their own share amounts to exit.\n    function _poc_ProgressiveCurve_previewWithdrawPanicAfterMint() internal {\n        uint256 totalShares = 1e18;\n        uint256 totalAssets = progressiveCurve.previewMint(totalShares, 0, 0);\n        assertEq(totalAssets, 1e18);\n\n        uint256 N = 5;\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n            uint256 cost = progressiveCurve.previewMint(1, totalShares, totalAssets);\n            totalShares += 1;\n            totalAssets += cost;\n        }\n\n        uint256 excessLocked = N;\n\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        progressiveCurve.previewWithdraw(totalAssets, totalAssets, totalShares);\n\n        uint256 maxWithdrawable = totalAssets - excessLocked;\n        uint256 sharesToBurn = progressiveCurve.previewWithdraw(maxWithdrawable, totalAssets, totalShares);\n        assertGt(sharesToBurn, 0);\n\n        uint256 redeemableAssets = progressiveCurve.previewRedeem(totalShares, totalShares, totalAssets);\n        assertGt(redeemableAssets, 0);\n        assertLt(redeemableAssets, totalAssets);\n    }\n\n    // HIGH-1 (variant): OffsetProgressiveCurve.previewWithdraw panics after previewMint\n    //\n    // OffsetProgressiveCurve.previewMint  (L136): area = squareUp(sNext) - square(s)\n    // OffsetProgressiveCurve.previewWithdraw (L160): inner = sub(square(s), deduct)\n    //\n    // The bug is structurally identical to PC. With offset=0, OPC is equivalent to PC\n    // and panics under the same conditions. For the production offset=5e17 the OFFSET^2\n    // buffer (0.25e18) delays the panic until ~2.5e17 excess-accumulating mints; the\n    // code path and fix are identical regardless.\n    //\n    // We demonstrate the panic with offset=0 to show OPC's code at L160 is directly\n    // vulnerable. Any future deployment of OPC with a small or zero offset is immediately\n    // exploitable.\n    function _poc_OffsetProgressiveCurve_previewWithdrawPanicAfterMint() internal {\n        OffsetProgressiveCurve opcImpl = new OffsetProgressiveCurve();\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy proxy = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(\n            address(opcImpl),\n            users.admin,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(OffsetProgressiveCurve.initialize.selector, \"OPC-zero-offset\", 2e18, 0)\n        );\n        OffsetProgressiveCurve opc = OffsetProgressiveCurve(address(proxy));\n\n        uint256 totalShares = 1e18;\n        uint256 totalAssets = opc.previewMint(totalShares, 0, 0);\n        assertEq(totalAssets, 1e18);\n\n        uint256 cost = opc.previewMint(1, totalShares, totalAssets);\n        totalShares += 1;\n        totalAssets += cost;\n\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        opc.previewWithdraw(totalAssets, totalAssets, totalShares);\n\n        uint256 redeemableAssets = opc.previewRedeem(totalShares, totalShares, totalAssets);\n        assertGt(redeemableAssets, 0);\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nRun POC:\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract PoCCore --match-test submissionValidity -v\n```",
